{
	"about": "An address the app was opened with, and whether the plugin hands it to the page, which reads it as a pasted link, says so when it is not one, and asks the owner before anything is used (openedLink in Paired.kt and Paired.swift). Android is opened with an address of the web (an App Link of Pine's own service, or a view intent another app sends it by name): one on http or https with a host, whose fragment begins with pair=. iOS is opened with the app's own scheme: pine://pair? and something after it. On both, printable ASCII only (no control character, no space) and at most 1024 characters, more than any pairing link has. input is the address, or null. expect is true (handed to the page as it is) or false (dropped).",
